---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE, CONTACT, ACTIVE_ADDRESS } from '../data/site';

const breadcrumbs = [{ name: 'Privacy', url: '/privacy/' }];
---

<Page
  title="Privacy Policy — John Bald Funeral Directors"
  heading="Privacy policy"
  description="How John Bald Funeral Directors collects, uses and protects your personal information."
  standfirst="What we collect, why, how long we keep it, and what you can ask us to do with it."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <p>
    John Bald Funeral Directors is part of {SITE.parentCompany}, which is the data
    controller for the information described here.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect, and why</h2>

  <h3>If you send us a message through this website</h3>
  <p>
    Your name, email address, telephone number if you give one, and whatever you write in
    the message. We use it only to reply to you. We do not add you to a mailing list and
    we do not pass it to anyone else.
  </p>

  <h3>If we arrange a funeral for you</h3>
  <p>
    We hold information about you and about the person who has died, because we cannot
    arrange a funeral without it — names, addresses, dates, next of kin, and the details
    required by registrars, crematoria and cemeteries.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some of this is what data protection law calls special category data, including
    information about health and about religious belief where that affects the funeral.
    We handle it on the basis that it is necessary to provide the service you have asked
    us for, and we treat it with the same discretion we treat everything else you tell us.
  </p>

  <h3>If you record your funeral wishes with us</h3>
  <p>
    We keep what you tell us so that it can be followed. You may change or withdraw it at
    any time by telling us.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>Only where it is necessary to carry out the funeral:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Registrars, crematoria and cemetery authorities</li>
    <li>The minister, priest or celebrant conducting the service</li>
    <li>Newspapers, where you have asked us to place a notice</li>
    <li>Golden Charter, where a funeral plan is involved</li>
    <li>Social Security Scotland, where you have asked us to help with a claim</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not sell your information. We do not share it for marketing. We do not pass it
    to insurers, will writers, estate agents or anyone else who might find a recently
    bereaved family commercially interesting.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Funeral records are kept for as long as we are required to, and in practice
    indefinitely — families come back years later asking where a relative's ashes were
    scattered or which lair was used, and it matters that we can tell them.
  </p>
  <p>
    Website enquiries that do not lead to a funeral are deleted once the conversation has
    finished.
  </p>

  <h2>Website analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We use privacy-first analytics that count visits without setting cookies, without
    tracking you across other websites, and without collecting anything that identifies
    you. That is why this site has no cookie banner — there is nothing to consent to.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>You may ask us to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Tell you what we hold about you</li>
    <li>Correct anything that is wrong</li>
    <li>Delete information, where we are not required to keep it</li>
    <li>Restrict what we do with it</li>
    <li>Provide it in a portable form</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Ask by telephoning{' '}
    <a href={CONTACT.phoneHref} class="font-semibold">{CONTACT.phone}</a>, emailing{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>, or writing to us at{' '}
    {ACTIVE_ADDRESS.street}, {ACTIVE_ADDRESS.locality}, {ACTIVE_ADDRESS.postcode}.
  </p>

  <h2>Complaints</h2>
  <p>
    Please tell us first — we would rather put something right than have you go elsewhere
    with it. If you are not satisfied, you may complain to the Information Commissioner's
    Office at ico.org.uk or on 0303 123 1113.
  </p>
</Page>

<!--
  Before launch: confirm the ICO registration number and the data controller's
  registered details with the client, and agree a written retention period for
  website enquiries with whoever operates the form handler.
-->
